    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** (74.73) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) leading the charge as our strongest plays. Both hitters benefit from favorable matchups against RHP Leahy and RHP Avila, respectively, with **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s outlook bolstered significantly by 10% wind-out conditions and a clean batting order spot. **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) also presents a high-ceiling option against the volatile Whisenhunt, capitalizing on a strong wind-out boost and a prime #2 slot. While **Gunnar Henderson** (64.32) is tasked with a difficult matchup against the elite arm of Kirby, his dynamic platoon advantage and projected top-of-the-order status keep him safely in our utility slot, maintaining our commitment to high-OPS production despite the pitching risk.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Brayan Rocchio**, whose 51.22 score narrowly missed the cut. While **Brayan Rocchio** offers solid stability, he was ultimately outperformed by the high-upside profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci**; despite the latter\u2019s struggles against LHP Rod\u00f3n, the team prioritizes the potential SB volume inherent in our current defensive configuration. Caution is advised with **Kyle Tucker** (62.52) and **Andy Pages** (60.42) as they face the formidable McClanahan; their scores remain above our 60-point threshold, but they face a significant SP skill penalty. We are monitoring the status of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" designation introduces volatility into our projected efficiency. Managers should ensure all rostered players confirm their status to avoid the \"below-floor\" trap, particularly with **Sam Antonacci** operating near his usage limits against a tough southpaw.",
